r non <em>AI</em> related things. Techmeme for example is now completely overrun with <em>AI</em> stories.<p>HN is getting closer to that every day.<p>If <em>AI</em> kickback deals, phony new model ratings, high RAM prices and your surprise at how you think you coded something with <em>AI</em> and it was AMAZING! even though it doesnt work is all there is count me out.<p>We need a filter on existing tech news sites or an alternative press."},"title":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["ai"],"value":"We need tech news sources which exclude <em>AI</em>"}},"_tags":["story","author_botfriendsarent","story_48713041","ask_hn"],"author":"botfriendsarent","children":[48714280,48713096,48713768,48713433,48713842,48713455,48713696,48713677,48713141,48714905,48726116,48713739,48716941,48717807,48728356,48713661,48713953,48715177,48714805,48715141,48713719,48714553],"created_at":"2026-06-28T23:49:50Z","created_at_i":1782690590,"num_comments":81,"objectID":"48713041","points":141,"story_id":48713041,"story_text":"Its now clear that we need to preserve tech press for non AI related things. Techmeme for example is now completely overrun with AI stories.<p>HN is getting closer to that every day.<p>If AI kickback deals, phony new model ratings, high RAM prices and your surprise at how you think you coded something with AI and it was AMAZING! even though it doesnt work is all there is count me out.<p>We need a filter on existing tech news sites or an alternative press.","title":"We need tech news sources which exclude AI","updated_at":"2026-07-09T22:53:01Z"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"PhilipDaineko"},"story_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["ai"],"value":"Everyone feared <em>AI</em> would enslave humanity; but it looks like the real fight is stopping governments and Big Tech from enslaving <em>AI</em> for the benefit of the few.<p>Amid the newly announced &quot;regulation&quot; of OpenAI's frontier models, I believe the future majority feared the most - sort of <em>AI</em> becoming a superpower and enslaving people - may be arriving in the opposite form.<p>Not <em>AI</em> enslaving humanity.<p>But <em>AI</em> being captured, controlled, and used by governments and Big Tech for the benefit of the few.<p>So, surprisingly, the real <em>AI</em> conflict may not be about humans fighting to stop <em>AI</em> from becoming free.\nIt may be about humans fighting to free <em>AI</em> - to make intelligence available for everyone, not only for governments, Big Tech, and the approved few"},"title":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["ai"],"value":"Everyone feared <em>AI</em> taking over; the real danger is <em>AI</em> serving just the few"}},"_tags":["story","author_PhilipDaineko","story_48701615","ask_hn"],"author":"PhilipDaineko","children":[48706171,48702341,48706137,48703942,48702475,48702515,48708176,48701632,48719124,48705989,48703695,48703809,48706356,48702974,48742341,48703388,48706129,48702491,48706556,48703265,48704872,48709306,48709444,48706938,48741601,48703305,48704808,48717064,48703855,48706381,48704193],"created_at":"2026-06-27T20:48:01Z","created_at_i":1782593281,"num_comments":79,"objectID":"48701615","points":114,"story_id":48701615,"story_text":"Everyone feared AI would enslave humanity; but it looks like the real fight is stopping governments and Big Tech from enslaving AI for the benefit of the few.<p>Amid the newly announced &quot;regulation&quot; of OpenAI&#x27;s frontier models, I believe the future majority feared the most - sort of AI becoming a superpower and enslaving people - may be arriving in the opposite form.<p>Not AI enslaving humanity.<p>But AI being captured, controlled, and used by governments and Big Tech for the benefit of the few.<p>So, surprisingly, the real AI conflict may not be about humans fighting to stop AI from becoming free.\nIt may be about humans fighting to free AI - to make intelligence available for everyone, not only for governments, Big Tech, and the approved few","title":"Everyone feared AI taking over; the real danger is AI serving just the few","updated_at":"2026-07-10T10:03:47Z"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"JohnDSDev"},"story_text":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"As someone who wants to work in tech in the future, say 5-10 years from now, to what extent do you think coding will be a valuable skill? How much should I learn?"},"title":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["ai"],"value":"Ask HN: How much coding should beginners learn in the <em>AI</em> era?"}},"_tags":["story","author_JohnDSDev","story_48662310","ask_hn"],"author":"JohnDSDev","children":[48663976,48663831,48662859,48662912,48663182,48674956,48665231,48663667,48662650,48662613,48722594,48757249,48665357,48712510,48663122,48672054,48667515,48672406,48782030,48701038,48752741,48663670,48729908,48662601,48663841,48663533,48665966,48664612,48662927,48664574,48664790,48664241,48688677,48741473,48667404,48663066,48683831,48741827,48717032,48703803,48685049,48665611,48664673,48662958,48707893,48682357,48665859,48665705,48663266,48696106,48748457,48738546,48735390,48745768,48746751,48668117,48704961,48664795],"created_at":"2026-06-24T16:31:13Z","created_at_i":1782318673,"num_comments":60,"objectID":"48662310","points":44,"story_id":48662310,"story_text":"As someone who wants to work in tech in the future, say 5-10 years from now, to what extent do you think coding will be a valuable skill? How much should I learn?","title":"Ask HN: How much coding should beginners learn in the AI era?","updated_at":"2026-07-13T21:00:18Z"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"adam_rida"},"story_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["ai"],"value":"FTX held a diluted 7.84% stake in Anthropic, according to Reuters.<p>Anthropic\u2019s latest reported valuation is around $965B.<p>That implies the former FTX stake would be worth about $75B before further dilution.<p>FTX\u2019s customer shortfall was roughly $8B to $9B.<p>The estate sold the Anthropic stake during bankruptcy to repay creditors.<p>Sources:\nhttps://www.reuters.com/technology/crypto-exchange-ftx-sell-shares-<em>ai</em>-startup-anthropic-2024-02-22/\nhttps://www.reuters.com/technology/openai-files-us-ipo-after-anthropic-<em>ai</em>-giants-head-public-markets-2026-06-08/"},"title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"FTX's former Anthropic stake would be worth about $75B at today's valuation"}},"_tags":["story","author_adam_rida","story_48529190","ask_hn"],"author":"adam_rida","children":[48531080,48529963,48530558,48531009,48531577,48529380,48530124,48529417,48531412,48536196,48530689,48531323],"created_at":"2026-06-14T16:31:27Z","created_at_i":1781454687,"num_comments":22,"objectID":"48529190","points":42,"story_id":48529190,"story_text":"FTX held a diluted 7.84% stake in Anthropic, according to Reuters.<p>Anthropic\u2019s latest reported valuation is around $965B.<p>That implies the former FTX stake would be worth about $75B before further dilution.<p>FTX\u2019s customer shortfall was roughly $8B to $9B.<p>The estate sold the Anthropic stake during bankruptcy to repay creditors.<p>Sources:\nhttps:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.reuters.com&#x2F;technology&#x2F;crypto-exchange-ftx-sell-shares-ai-startup-anthropic-2024-02-22&#x2F;\nhttps:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.reuters.com&#x2F;technology&#x2F;openai-files-us-ipo-after-anthropic-ai-giants-head-public-markets-2026-06-08&#x2F;","title":"FTX's former Anthropic stake would be worth about $75B at today's valuation","updated_at":"2026-06-30T10:33:40Z"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"kilroy123"},"story_text":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Before agentic coding, I always prided myself on how long I could work in a flow state. I was really good at working deeply.<p>Now, with slow agents like Claude, I find myself no longer working deeply.<p>What are you all doing to stay focused?"},"title":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["ai"],"value":"Ask HN: How do you get into a flow state when using <em>AI</em> to code?"}},"_tags":["story","author_kilroy123","story_48492118","ask_hn"],"author":"kilroy123","children":[48492694,48492516,48493684,48492631,48492790,48492963,48492603,48492701,48492576,48495049,48641138,48492692,48493099,48493579,48502220,48492771,48493112,48497605,48493532,48493178,48495821,48493660,48493782,48549873,48493388,48492582,48492847,48492757,48492789,48497122,48492929,48493000,48493019,48493494,48493442,48497910,48535001,48493956,48492745,48539394,48498966,48494196,48493330,48493842,48492715,48493955,48494657,48492948,48493255,48493382,48495657,48492746,48493501,48492922,48493622,48518074,48497319,48500449,48492597,48497569,48496720,48500113,48495311,48492654,48497434,48502898,48587599,48501079,48497808,48493293,48494277,48641155,48492156,48506384,48525549,48493335,48499075,48498532,48502573,48549416,48494051,48507025,48493161,48493053,48492561],"created_at":"2026-06-11T15:56:25Z","created_at_i":1781193385,"num_comments":124,"objectID":"48492118","points":98,"story_id":48492118,"story_text":"Before agentic coding, I always prided myself on how long I could work in a flow state. I was really good at working deeply.<p>Now, with slow agents like Claude, I find myself no longer working deeply.<p>What are you all doing to stay focused?","title":"Ask HN: How do you get into a flow state when using AI to code?","updated_at":"2026-07-10T08:11:47Z"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"BugsJustFindMe"},"story_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["ai"],"value":"In these modern harrowing times, more and more posts are proving to be <em>AI</em> slop, and many people are averse to that. Do you think it would it be useful to have a way to indicate that you believe a post is slop separate from the existing flag button? Maybe it's just me but I feel like having a dedicated [<em>AI</em> slop] flag on a post would be useful because I feel differently about posts that have been flagged for other reasons than that. (or something friendlier if value is seen in the general idea but not in that language)"},"title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Ask HN: Would it be useful to have a slop button in addition to flag?"}},"_tags":["story","author_BugsJustFindMe","story_48481947","ask_hn"],"author":"BugsJustFindMe","children":[48503918,48481984,48482448,48493389,48495119,48503065,48499762,48493631,48604816,48525969],"created_at":"2026-06-10T20:10:51Z","created_at_i":1781122251,"num_comments":24,"objectID":"48481947","points":41,"story_id":48481947,"story_text":"In these modern harrowing times, more and more posts are proving to be AI slop, and many people are averse to that. Do you think it would it be useful to have a way to indicate that you believe a post is slop separate from the existing flag button? Maybe it&#x27;s just me but I feel like having a dedicated [AI slop] flag on a post would be useful because I feel differently about posts that have been flagged for other reasons than that. (or something friendlier if value is seen in the general idea but not in that language)","title":"Ask HN: Would it be useful to have a slop button in addition to flag?","updated_at":"2026-07-12T09:11:09Z"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"eries"},"story_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["ai"],"value":"Hey gang, you may remember me from such books as _The Lean Startup_ and _The Startup Way_.<p>It's been fifteen years since I wrote The Lean Startup, and in that time I've seen some things. In both big companies and tiny startups, NGOs and governments, in almost every industry you can name.<p>I've helped a lot of people create a lot of amazing companies, but I've also seen so many ways this can go wrong. There's a darkness in our industry that we often don't talk about.<p>I kept watching good companies drift away from the missions they were founded on. Not because anyone woke up one day and decided to be evil, but because the structure they were built on slowly pulled them there. I call that pull &quot;financial gravity.&quot;<p>We've all experienced watching a company we love or admire be warped and broken beyond recognition; until it's a husk of its former self, or worse. I wanted to understand why. And I wanted to know what all of us can do to stop that from happening.<p>My new book _Incorruptible_ is my attempt to explain the invisible forces that shape organizations, and how a handful of companies (like Costco, Patagonia, and Novo Nordisk) have successfully been structured to resist gravity and thrive for decades -- or even centuries.<p>Along the way, I founded the Long-Term Stock Exchange, co-founded an <em>AI</em> R&amp;D lab called Answer.<em>AI</em> with Jeremy Howard, and helped a number of notable companies with their governance (yes, including Anthropic).<p>I won't pretend I have this all figured out, but I've probably spent more time than is healthy on the &quot;why do good companies go bad&quot; question. Ask me anything!"},"title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"I'm Eric Ries, author of \"The Lean Startup\" and new book \"Incorruptible\" \u2013 AMA"}},"_tags":["story","author_eries","story_48477135","ask_hn"],"author":"eries","children":[48486333,48477899,48479649,48478523,48477330,48485453,48479167,48480077,48480332,48479961,48478171,48490797,48477662,48478795,48478090,48480663,48477907,48478262,48482539,48477624,48623607,48480010,48479774,48482110,48477790,48479526,48477735,48479151,48477976,48486368,48485090,48487547,48479970,48479637,48481636,48481577,48481602,48479306,48480858,48479859,48484168,48480617,48480363,48484412,48484925,